{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"humdrum-priestly-lcont","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n\n`reduce_all_tickets` (src/rebar/reducer/_api.py) applies `exclude_deleted` and `exclude_session_logs` only after its loop finishes, and callers filter only after it returns, so every ticket that will be discarded is held in memory until then. Code reviews are 3,439 of 9,727 store directories. Measured on an isolated copy of the live store, 2026-10-29 (tracemalloc peak during the call, current caches):\n\n| Read | Peak now | Peak with an in-loop filter and field trim | Output compared |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `search` (`reads.py` `search_state`, full state, 141 matches) | 348.8 MB | 24.6 MB | identical (141 = 141) |\n| `recent_session_logs` (full state, keeps 5) | 284.3 MB | 10.8 MB | identical |\n| `bridge_fsck` binding-drift step (uses ticket_id, status, archived) | 328.6 MB | 69.5 MB (66.3 MB of it is binding/Jira data) | drift counts identical |\n| `validate` (full-body list) | 284.3 MB | 49.3 MB | report identical |\n| `ticket_deps` on a graph-cache miss | 284.9 MB | 64.2 MB | not compared |\n| `list_tickets --status=open` | 64.1 MB | 11.0 MB | ids identical |\n| `list_tickets` with `blocking_state` (holds pass 1 during `find_ready_tickets`) | 106.6 MB | not prototyped | — |\n\nI confirmed the `search_state` and `recent_session_logs_state` calls and the post-loop filters by reading the code.\n\n## Plan\n1. Give `reduce_all_tickets` an optional per-ticket keep predicate, and apply the existing exclusions inside the loop so a discarded ticket is never retained.\n2. Move each caller above onto the predicate plus an `omit_fields` projection limited to the fields it reads. Search matches inside the loop and keeps only matches. recent_session_logs keeps (id, created_at) and re-reduces the top N.\n3. For each caller, add a test that compares output with the old path on a fixture store, and a test that asserts the projection is applied.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Each read in the table returns output identical to the current code on a fixture covering archived, deleted, session_log and code_review tickets.\n- [ ] Each read's peak traced memory on a clone of the live store is recorded on this ticket before and after.\n- [ ] `reduce_all_tickets` retains no ticket that a caller's exclusions discard.\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- src/rebar/reducer/_api.py\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py\n- src/rebar/graph/_loader.py\n- src/rebar/_commands/bridge_fsck_drift.py","id":"d70a-97d9-7f05-4293","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Store-wide MCP reads hold every ticket in full until the loop ends"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793301687583935001,"uuid":"96dd518d-3321-43d9-8a66-52b0acd831aa"}